    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If a horizontal line has the equation $$f(x) = a$$ and a vertical line has the equation $$x = a,$$ what is the point of intersection? Explain why what you found is the point of intersection.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The point of intersection is $$( a,a ). ( a,a ).$$ This is because for the horizontal line, all of the $$y y$$ coordinates are $$a a$$ and for the vertical line, all of the $$x x$$ coordinates are $$a. a.$$ The point of intersection is on both lines and therefore will have these two characteristics.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
