        <paragraph>A city’s population in the year 1960 was 287,500. In 1989 the population was 275,900. Compute the rate of growth of the population and make a statement about the population rate of change in people per year.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The slope is –400. this means for every year between 1960 and 1989, the population dropped by 400 per year in the city.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
